IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha-types`

-- Holidays Act 2003 — GOAL 1: THE PAY MEASURES.
--
--   "What is the employee's ordinary weekly pay, relevant or average daily
--    pay, gross earnings over a period, and average weekly earnings?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_129.txt — ss 5, 8, 9,
-- 9A, 10, 10A, 11, 14, 16(3), 22(3).

§ `Goal 1 — the pay measures`

§§ `Board or lodgings (s 10)`

-- s 10(1) "includes the cash value of any board or lodgings provided by an
-- employer to the employee— (a) as agreed by the employer and employee; or
-- (b) as determined by a Labour Inspector". (2) "Despite subsection (1), ...
-- does not include the cash value ... (a) if the work done by the employee
-- requires the employee to stay overnight in a residence other than the
-- employee's usual place of residence; or (b) if the board or lodgings are
-- provided because of special circumstances."
@ref s 10
GIVEN b IS A MAYBE `Board or lodgings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cash value of board or lodgings counted` b MEANS
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF     x's `the work requires staying overnight away from the usual residence`
            OR x's `provided because of special circumstances`
        THEN 0
        ELSE x's `cash value agreed or determined`

§§ `Gross earnings (ss 10A, 14)`

-- s 14 "(a) means all payments that the employer is required to pay to the
-- employee under the employee's employment agreement, including ...; but (b)
-- excludes any payments that the employer is not bound ... to pay ...; and
-- (c) also excludes". s 10A "(a) includes payments made to the employee
-- under section 14 of the Home and Community Support (Payment for Travel
-- Between Clients) Settlement Act 2016; but (b) excludes payments made ...
-- under section 19".
@ref ss 10A, 14
GIVEN k IS A `Payment kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts toward gross earnings` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `(a)(i) salary or wages` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(a)(ii) an allowance, other than a non-taxable reimbursement of actual costs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(a)(iii) pay for a holiday or leave taken in the period` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(a)(iv) a productivity or incentive-based payment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(a)(v) a payment for overtime` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(a)(vi) the cash value of board or lodgings agreed or determined under s 10` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(a)(vii) first week compensation under s 97 of the Accident Compensation Act 2001` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(b)(i) a discretionary payment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `(b)(ii) weekly compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 2001` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `(b)(iii) a payment for absence on volunteers leave` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `(c)(i) a reimbursement of actual costs` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `(c)(ii) a reimbursement of a reasonably assessed amount of costs` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `(c)(iii) an employer contribution to a superannuation scheme` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `(c)(iv) a payment for annual holidays paid out under s 28B` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 10A(a) a payment under s 14 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 10A(b) a payment under s 19 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016` THEN FALSE

@ref ss 10A, 14
@export The employee's gross earnings over a period under s 14 of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ): the payments the employment agreement binds the employer to make, without discretionary payments, ACC weekly compensation, volunteers leave pay, reimbursements, superannuation contributions and annual holidays paid out under s 28B. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF Payment  @desc Each payment made in the period, with its kind under s 14 (or s 10A) and its amount
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gross earnings in` payments MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD IF `counts toward gross earnings` (p's `kind of payment`) THEN p's `amount of the payment` ELSE 0) payments)

§§ `Ordinary weekly pay (s 8)`

-- s 8(1) "(a) means the amount of pay that the employee receives under his
-- or her employment agreement for an ordinary working week; and (b)
-- includes— (i) productivity or incentive-based payments (including
-- commission) if those payments are a regular part of the employee's pay:
-- (ii) payments for overtime if those payments are a regular part of the
-- employee's pay: (iii) the cash value of any board or lodgings provided by
-- the employer to the employee". The exclusions in (c) are the amounts not
-- given as inputs.
@ref s 8(1), s 10
GIVEN f IS A `Weekly pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ordinary weekly pay under s 8(1)` f MEANS
        f's `pay for an ordinary working week`
    PLUS f's `regular productivity or incentive-based payments`
    PLUS f's `regular overtime`
    PLUS `the cash value of board or lodgings counted` (f's `board or lodgings in the week`)

-- s 8(2) "If it is not possible to determine an employee's ordinary weekly
-- pay under subsection (1), the pay must be calculated in accordance with
-- the following formula: (a − b) ÷ c where— a is the employee's gross
-- earnings for— (i) the 4 calendar weeks before the end of the pay period
-- immediately before the calculation is made; or (ii) if the employee's
-- normal pay period is longer than 4 weeks, that pay period ... b is the
-- total amount of payments described in subsection (1)(c)(i) to (iii) c is
-- 4." The converted text has lost the formula's symbols; see BRIEF.md.
-- FORK F1: c is 4 even where (a)(ii) takes a pay period longer than 4 weeks.
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN f IS A `Weekly pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ordinary weekly pay under s 8(2)` f MEANS
    (f's `gross earnings for the s 8(2) period` MINUS f's `payments described in s 8(1)(c)(i) to (iii) in that period`) DIVIDED BY 4

-- s 8(3) "However, an employment agreement may specify a special rate of
-- ordinary weekly pay ... if the rate is equal to, or greater than, what
-- would otherwise be calculated under subsection (1) or subsection (2)."
-- A lower special rate reduces the entitlement and has no effect (s 6(3)).
@ref s 8, s 6(3)
@export The employee's ordinary weekly pay under s 8 of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ), for annual holiday pay: the pay for an ordinary working week with regular incentive payments, regular overtime and board or lodgings (s 8(1)); if that cannot be determined, (gross earnings for the last 4 weeks less irregular and one-off payments) divided by 4 (s 8(2)); or an agreed special rate if it is not lower (s 8(3)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Weekly pay facts`  @desc Whether ordinary weekly pay can be determined under s 8(1); the pay for an ordinary week, regular incentive payments and overtime, board or lodgings; gross earnings and irregular payments for the s 8(2) period; any special rate in the agreement
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinary weekly pay` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `special rate of ordinary weekly pay in the agreement`
    WHEN JUST special THEN IF special AT LEAST calculated THEN special ELSE calculated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN calculated
    WHERE
        calculated MEANS
            IF   f's `it is possible to determine ordinary weekly pay under s 8(1)`
            THEN `ordinary weekly pay under s 8(1)` f
            ELSE `ordinary weekly pay under s 8(2)` f

§§ `Relevant daily pay and average daily pay (ss 9, 9A)`

-- s 9(1) "(a) means the amount of pay that the employee would have received
-- had the employee worked on the day concerned; and (b) includes— (i)
-- productivity or incentive-based payments ... (ii) payments for overtime
-- ... (iii) the cash value of any board or lodgings". (1A) a special rate
-- "if the rate is equal to, or greater than, the rate that would otherwise
-- be calculated under subsection (1)". (2) the amount "does not include any
-- amount that would be added by virtue of section 50(1)(a)".
@ref ss 9, 10
GIVEN f IS A `Daily pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the relevant daily pay` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `special rate of relevant daily pay in the agreement`
    WHEN JUST special THEN IF special AT LEAST calculated THEN special ELSE calculated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN calculated
    WHERE
        calculated MEANS
                f's `pay the employee would have received had they worked the day`
           PLUS `the cash value of board or lodgings counted` (f's `board or lodgings on the day`)

-- s 9A(2) "a ÷ b where— a is the employee's gross earnings for the 52
-- calendar weeks before the end of the pay period immediately before the
-- calculation is made b is the number of whole or part days during which the
-- employee earned those gross earnings, including any day on which the
-- employee was on a paid holiday or paid leave; but excluding any other day
-- on which the employee did not actually work."
@ref s 9A(2)
GIVEN f IS A `Daily pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average daily pay` f MEANS
    IF   f's `whole or part days on which those earnings were earned` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN f's `gross earnings for the 52 weeks before the last pay period ended` DIVIDED BY f's `whole or part days on which those earnings were earned`
    ELSE `no days were worked in the 52 weeks, so s 9A(2) gives no average daily pay; a Labour Inspector may determine it under s 11`

`no days were worked in the 52 weeks, so s 9A(2) gives no average daily pay; a Labour Inspector may determine it under s 11` MEANS
    REFUSE "no days were worked in the 52 weeks, so s 9A(2) gives no average daily pay; a Labour Inspector may determine it under s 11"

-- s 9A(1) "An employer may use an employee's average daily pay ... if— (a)
-- it is not possible or practicable to determine an employee's relevant
-- daily pay under section 9(1); or (b) the employee's daily pay varies
-- within the pay period when the holiday or leave falls."
@ref s 9A(1)
GIVEN f IS A `Daily pay facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may use average daily pay` f IF
        NOT f's `it is possible and practicable to determine relevant daily pay`
    OR  f's `the employee's daily pay varies within the pay period`

-- ss 49, 60, 71, 72I pay "the employee's relevant daily pay or average daily
-- pay". FORK F2: where relevant daily pay cannot be determined, average
-- daily pay is the only measure left; where it can, average daily pay is
-- used only if s 9A(1)(b) applies and the employer chooses it.
@ref ss 9, 9A
@export The daily pay for a public holiday, alternative holiday, or a day of sick, bereavement or family violence leave under ss 9 and 9A of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ): relevant daily pay (what the employee would have received had they worked the day, with incentive payments, overtime and board, or an agreed special rate if not lower), or average daily pay (52 weeks' gross earnings divided by the days on which they were earned) where s 9A allows it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Daily pay facts`  @desc Whether relevant daily pay can be determined; what the employee would have received on the day; board; a special rate; whether daily pay varies in the pay period and the employer chooses average daily pay; 52 weeks' gross earnings and the days on which they were earned
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily pay` f MEANS
    IF      NOT f's `it is possible and practicable to determine relevant daily pay`
    THEN    `the average daily pay` f
    ELSE IF `the employer may use average daily pay` f AND f's `the employer chooses average daily pay`
    THEN    `the average daily pay` f
    ELSE    `the relevant daily pay` f

§§ `Average weekly earnings (ss 5, 16(3), 22(3))`

-- s 16(2)(a)(vi) "on unpaid leave for any other reason for a period of no
-- more than 1 week". FORK F3: a longer period of other unpaid leave is left
-- out whole, not only the days beyond the first week.
@ref s 16(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Absence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence counts toward the 12 months` a IF
    CONSIDER a's `kind of absence`
    WHEN `other unpaid leave` THEN
            a's `length in days` AT MOST 7
        OR  a's `agreed to be included in the 12 months`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The days an absence adds to the 12 months under s 16(1).
@ref s 16(1)-(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Absence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days the absence defers the anniversary` a MEANS
    IF `the absence counts toward the 12 months` a THEN 0 ELSE a's `length in days`

-- s 16(3) "If ... an employer and employee agree that any period of unpaid
-- leave of more than 1 week is to be included in the employee's 12 months of
-- continuous employment, the divisor of 52 ... must be reduced by the number
-- of whole or part weeks greater than 1 week that the employee was on the
-- unpaid leave."
@ref s 16(3)
GIVEN a IS AN Absence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks s 16(3) takes off the divisor for` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `kind of absence`
    WHEN `other unpaid leave` THEN
        IF     a's `agreed to be included in the 12 months`
           AND a's `length in days` GREATER THAN 7
        THEN CEILING ((a's `length in days` MINUS 7) DIVIDED BY 7)
        ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 0

@ref s 16(3)
GIVEN absences IS A LIST OF Absence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` absences MEANS
    52 MINUS sum (map `the weeks s 16(3) takes off the divisor for` absences)

-- s 5 "average weekly earnings means 1/52 of an employee's gross earnings".
@ref ss 5, 16(3)
GIVEN gross IS A NUMBER, absences IS A LIST OF Absence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average weekly earnings over 12 months, gross` gross `, absences` absences MEANS
    gross DIVIDED BY `the divisor for 12 months, after s 16(3), given` absences
